                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Drugs crossing the Southern Border are endangering our communities! From devastating individual health to jeopardizing public safety and societal well-being, the impact is profound. In 2023, drug overdoses claimed over 112,000 American lives, hitting young people hard. #SyntheticOpioids like Fentanyl, Methadone, and Tramadol are key players in this tragic surge, as reported by the @CDCgov .\n\nThe ripple effects? Increased crime, compromised community safety, and a heavy toll on our healthcare and legal systems. And the profit for cartels? A staggering $5B to $30B from these nefarious activities. It's time to acknowledge the cost of inaction.\n\n#AmericaFirst means tackling this crisis head-on. @A1Policy @BrookeLRollins @DHSgov @CBP @ChadFWolf @HeidiOverton @ashleyhayek",
